  "interpretation": {
    "correction": "Section 10's frozen wording says cap choice 'does not matter'. That is an equivalence claim the design cannot support: the primary endpoint tested for a difference and found none, which is not the same thing. The frozen text is preserved above as provenance and the corrected reading is what the paper states.",
    "frozen_reading_verbatim": "cap choice does not matter at this budget; W2's censoring finding stands as accounting only, and the paper says the reallocation was tried and did not pay",
    "frozen_row": "all three within noise",
    "reported_reading": "No detectable difference in held-out verification success. This is NOT an equivalence result: no equivalence test was performed, and the intervals still admit meaningful effects (split2-long [-0.075, 0.175], split3-long [-0.125, 0.075] in success proportion). What the data do show positively is that equal NOMINAL cap budgets were not equal REALIZED compute: realized completion tokens are higher for split2 and split3 (resolved, interval excludes zero); realized wall time is higher for split2 only, and the throughput differences are UNRESOLVED for both. The token result is the load-bearing one and it is the one that supports the paper's thesis.",
    "source": "spec/ALLOCATION_SPEC.md section 10"
  },
